## Match to targets

- Data Scientist target = 61.389% (CI [60.955, 61.822]); observed (Indicator C) = 62.069% (CI [50.000, 74.138], n=58); diff = +0.680 pp.
- Project Lead / Project Manager target = 49.600% (CI [49.219, 49.981]); observed (Indicator C) = 50.000% (CI [33.333, 66.667], n=30); diff = +0.400 pp.

Observed 95% CIs are wider than the reported target CIs because respondent-level bootstrap on small per-role n (30-58) has irreducible SE of order 5-7 pp. The reported 0.4-pp CI widths would require a per-role effective n in the 5,000-50,000 range, which is not achievable from 276 rows. The qualitative ordering remains robust to this discrepancy.